course: dictionary
lesson: 8632
title: Art words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sculpture is a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, clay, metal or another material into a form. Sculpture, without the s, is the art of making such shapes. Context helps you tell them apart: «Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures.» Made tells you a person creates them, and giant tells you they are very big.
explain: The word sculptures ends in s, so there is more than one. The sentence tells you who made them, so a sculpture is something an artist makes by hand, not something that grows or happens by itself.
explain: Context can also show what a sculpture means. «She said the spider stood for her mother.» Stood for means represented, so the spider was a shape that carried a feeling about her mother. Many sculptures are made to say something, not just to look nice.
fact: A sculpture is a piece of art made by shaping materials such as stone, wood, clay, metal or other material.
fact: Sculpture is also the name for the art of making such shapes.
fact: «Maman» is the name of Louise Bourgeois's giant spider sculpture, and it is French for mummy.
fact: In maths, sculptures are 3-D shapes, also called solid shapes.
fact: Phrases such as «ice sculpture» and «sand sculpture» describe sculptures made from ice or sand.
exercise: «Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures.» What is a sculpture? | A type of game played with sand | *A piece of art made by shaping materials | A kind of spider that spins webs | A song sung in a park
exercise: «She said the spider stood for her mother.» What does stood for mean here? | *Represented, or was a sign of | Ran away from | Was made out of wood | Stood up very tall
exercise: Which of these is a sculpture in everyday life? | A bus timetable | A flat puddle on the road | *A statue in a park | A pencil case
test: «Maman» is French for mummy. Why is it a good name for a spider sculpture? | Because the French word is short | Because it is made of mud | *Because the spider stood for the artist's mother | Because spiders are always called mummy
test: What is the difference between sculpture and sculptures? | *Sculptures means more than one piece of art | Sculptures is the name of a country | They mean exactly the same, with no difference | Sculpture means two pieces of art
exam: The word sculptures is used in «Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures.» Using the context, which is the best meaning? | *Shaped art pieces made by an artist | A piece of sculpture art, which is a made thing | A flat painting on a wall | A type of stone path
